from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P=R.parent
load=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
f=load(R/'FREEZE.json');a=load(R/'AUTHORED-CHECKS.json')
for n,h in f['local_sha256'].items():assert hashlib.sha256((R/n).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==h
for n,h in f['historical_sha256'].items():assert hashlib.sha256((P/n).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==h
q=load(P/'transition-maxT-qual-v98/QUALIFICATION.json');assert q['status']=='FAIL' and q['robustness_banks_not_run']==[2,3]
status=dict(status='FROZEN RETROSPECTIVE DESIGN; NOT QUALIFIED',authored_arithmetic=a['status'],full_sampler_and_nuisance_qualification='NOT RUN: qualification-only runner and complete control implementation freeze still required',actual_layout_power='NOT RUN',new_corrected_source_score='NOT COMPUTED',source_scoring='CLOSED',v98='FAIL unchanged; banks2/3 unrun',power_gate='Each of8panel/views: >=.80 at r1.5 and >=.90 at r2; all3newmethod banks required',full_search='All original pair columns, both signs, both middle views, unchanged x28 budget',exposure='Retrospective; historical source order and raw results already known')
(R/'STATUS.json').write_text(json.dumps(status,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
e=html.escape
body='''<p>VOYNICH · RETROSPECTIVE RESIDUAL ORDER · v103</p><h1>A test beyond the specified local transitions</h1>
<p class="notice"><strong>Design frozen. Full qualification pending. Manuscript scoring CLOSED.</strong> Earlier failures remain unchanged. No fresh holdout or independent confirmation is claimed.</p>
<h2>The question stays narrow</h2><p>Does <code>sh — one readable word — qok</code> exceed its conditional expectation after fixing each span’s adjacent sh/qok/other transition counts? Compare the reverse too. Keep Bath hand2/B/P and Starred hand3/B/P separate, H/F separately, and both original middle definitions. Unknowns block gaps; word boundaries are literal.</p>
<h2>Keep the family; change the tail scale</h2><p>v98 compared pilot-standardized count contrasts. The new candidate computes an exact conditional tail for every original contrast, then calibrates the smallest tail across the complete original family. This accounts for discreteness and asymmetric null shapes without selecting only sh/qok. It is a new candidate, with no promised power advantage.</p>
<ol><li><strong>Condition:</strong> pin literal endpoints, whole-word inventory, unknown seams and all nine sh/qok/other adjacent counts within each readable span.</li><li><strong>Count exactly:</strong> a signature DP retains local class plus A/B memberships, including overlap, to obtain every contrast’s exact gap-score distribution.</li><li><strong>Correct the full search:</strong> keep all original pair columns, both signs and both middle views; 4096 joint conditional calibration layouts; conservative plus-one minP and the unchanged ×28 budget.</li><li><strong>Require qualification:</strong> full sampler/null checks, then actual-layout power at the unchanged frozen effects. No pooling away a failed hand, reading, view or bank.</li></ol>
<p>Column counts remain 4005/4371 for Bath H/F and 9730/9316 for Starred H/F. Constant columns remain. Resource failures block the panel; no dropping difficult columns, reducing correction or substituting a normal tail.</p>
<h2>Qualification ledger</h2><table><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Status</th></tr><tr><td>Small authored DP/arithmetic checks</td><td>PASS: 5460 sequences; 2592 signature fibers; 5184 view histograms; three toy family orbits</td></tr><tr><td>Full sampler, family and nuisance-control qualification</td><td>NOT RUN — complete qualification runner/control freeze required</td></tr><tr><td>Actual-layout full-family power</td><td>NOT RUN</td></tr><tr><td>New corrected manuscript score</td><td>CLOSED / NOT COMPUTED</td></tr><tr><td>Earlier v98 qualification</td><td>FAIL preserved; banks2/3 remain unrun</td></tr></table>
<p>The prototype reads authored strings only, not manuscript files. It checks exact histograms, overlapping memberships, conservative tails, ties, duplicate-column invariance and small finite-orbit rank bounds. It does not establish full search calibration or manuscript-sized sensitivity.</p>
<h2>The power gates are unchanged</h2><p>For every one of the eight panel/views: at least <strong>80% power at weight1.5</strong> and <strong>90% at weight2</strong>. Preserve all low, reverse and partial-coverage cases, using the same v97 effects and hashed subsets. One failed first bank blocks later banks and scoring. All three new-method banks must pass independently. These do not resume v98’s failed attempt.</p>
<h2>What a result could establish</h2><p>A pass would identify residual order relative to this particular adjacent-class model. Position-dependent writing, extended collocation, copying, notation and other local mechanisms can still produce it. It would not establish grammar, meaning or exclusion of all junction effects. Adversarial controls preserve these mechanism-specificity limits.</p><p>Full-family calibration is asserted under the specified joint conditional law, not as unproved strong error control under arbitrary mixtures of individual nulls. Neither correction nor a new method erases the historical search. The new corrected score stays closed during qualification; the old raw source arrangements have already been seen.</p>
<h2>Frozen design and receipts</h2><p><a href="PROTOCOL.md">Complete protocol, algorithms and stop rules</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Pre-check source/code hashes</a> · <a href="EXPOSURE-CLARIFICATION.md">Historical exposure clarification</a> · <a href="AUTHORED-CHECKS.json">Authored checks</a> · <a href="STATUS.json">Explicit pending gates</a> · <a href="engine.py">Authored-only prototype</a> · <a href="../transition-maxT-qual-v98/report.html">Preserved v98 failure</a></p>
<p>Method references: <a href="https://gksmyth.github.io/pubs/PermPValuesPreprint.pdf">Phipson &amp; Smyth: finite Monte Carlo p-values</a>; <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3117234/">Westfall &amp; Troendle: multiple testing and closure</a>. They support the statistical cautions; they do not qualify this implementation.</p><p>Browser appearance unreviewed; source/hash and authored arithmetic checks are separate.</p>'''
css='<style>body{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:30px;background:#f5f2e9;color:#203f35;font:17px/1.6 system-ui}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:32px}.notice{background:#e0e9d8;padding:16px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #bac9bb}a{color:inherit}code{font-size:.94em}li{margin:10px 0}</style>'
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Retrospective residual order design · v103</title>'+css+'<main>'+body+'</main></html>',encoding='utf-8')
(R/'VERIFICATION.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(frozen_design_hashes='PASS',prior_receipt_hashes='PASS',authored_checks=a['status'],full_method='NOT QUALIFIED',source_power='NOT RUN',new_source_score='NOT COMPUTED',v98_gate='FAIL unchanged'),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
